      "description": "An automatic tool magazine is a storage system integrated with a CNC machine tool that holds cutting tools and enables automatic tool changes via the machine"s tool changer (ATC — Automatic Tool Changer). For titanium machining, large-capacity magazines (60-120 tools) are essential because titanium wears tools rapidly — typical tool life ranges from 15-45 minutes. A large magazine supports redundant sister tooling that the CNC control automatically switches to when the primary tool reaches its programmed life limit, enabling extended unattended "lights-out" operations.",
