    "entityDefinition": {
      "title": "What is a Wire EDM Machine?",
      "description": "A Wire Electrical Discharge Machine (Wire EDM) uses a thin electrically charged wire (typically 0.05-0.33 mm diameter brass or coated wire) to erode material through controlled electrical discharges. The wire and workpiece are submerged in deionized water dielectric, and there is no mechanical contact between tool and workpiece — eliminating cutting forces, tool deflection, and work hardening. For titanium, Wire EDM is the preferred method for cutting complex profiles, thin-wall features, sharp internal corners, and prototype geometries where conventional machining would cause deformation or residual stress.",
